---
<Base title="Loop Club — 16-track looper for MPC Sample | Kim’s Work" description={p.summary}>
<article class="wrap guide">
<a class="back" href={url('software/sample-mods/')}>← MPC Sample mods</a>
<p class="eyebrow">MPC SAMPLE · PUBLIC PREVIEW {p.version} · BY KIM</p>
<h1>Build a loop.<br/>Keep playing.</h1>
<p class="lead">Sixteen independent audio, synth and drum tracks. Record a phrase, finish at a bar and keep it looping while you build the next layer.</p>
<figure class="device-shot"><img src={url(`images/${p.image}`)} width="320" height="240" alt={p.imageAlt}/><figcaption>Actual MPC Sample screen · Native 320×240 display.</figcaption></figure>
<div class="manual-actions"><a class="button" href={p.download}>Download preview {p.version}</a><a href={url('mods/loop-club/manual/')}>Read the manual →</a><a href={p.release}>Release & SHA-256 ↗</a></div>
<p class="platform-note">MPC Sample firmware 1.3.0.12 only. An SD preload mod, not an MPC OS plugin or a firmware image. Preserve your existing autorun before installing.</p>
<h2>The looper comes first.</h2>
<p>Choose Audio / Synth / Drum. SHIFT+track pad starts recording; SHIFT+the same pad finishes at the next bar. The LOOP screen stays visible and ordinary pads play the selected source. REPLACE sets a new length; OVERDUB retains the old length. Each track keeps its own length: a one-bar part repeats alongside a four-bar phrase. DATA selects tracks; the fader follows with pickup. ERASE/COPY opens DELETE; SHIFT+ERASE/COPY opens COPY. B1–B3 select COPY / DELETE / MOVE; Undo/Redo protects the latest edit.</p>
<div class="feature-grid"><section><h3>Synth and stereo movement</h3><p>Two oscillators, individual Tune/Fine/Level, resonant filter and separate amp/filter ADSRs. A six-shape tempo-sync LFO moves Pitch and Filter. Tremolo, Auto Pan and Auto Filter are independent insert effects; legacy modulation values remain editable.</p></section><section><h3>Drums with room to shape</h3><p>Sixteen original procedural sounds, musical pattern generation and subdivision velocity accents. Two layers per sound with Volume, Tune, relative Shift, Decay and sample REV. Optional user banks stay outside the app. Import a Drum XPM by choosing its A–H bank; retain up to four original velocity/cycle/random zones under Layer1.</p></section><section><h3>Tap an effect. Keep the others.</h3><p>Track and master FX use 4×4 pad boards with momentary press/release and SHIFT-latched states. Two track effects stay on together without silent replacement. Master combines Dust, Drive, Squeeze, Wobble, Dub Echo, Duck and two custom FX; bypass keeps settings.</p></section><section><h3>Sidechain that follows your beat</h3><p>Use an individual drum or a whole track as the detector. Duck the other tracks, choose a custom target mask, or pump the full master. Depth, sensitivity, free/tempo-synced recovery and a reduction meter.</p></section></div>
<div class="screens-grid">{[['turntable','Tap PAD1 to toggle Grab; hold PAD2 to cut the scratch source'],['swing','Apply non-destructive Swing to every MIDI loop'],['midi','Record notes while retaining the original sample']].map(([name,alt])=><figure><img src={url(`images/loop-club-${name}-${name==='turntable'?'0.13.0':'0.11.1'}.webp`)} width="320" height="240" alt={alt} loading="lazy"/><figcaption>{alt}. Actual MPC Sample capture.</figcaption></figure>)}</div>
<h2 id="scratch-performance">A drum loop. A sample. A scratch.</h2>
<p>Scratch Pocket pairs an original drum groove with a Dm9 chord played and resampled inside Loop Club. Grab PAD 1, move the fader, record the gesture and let it loop back with the drums. Recorded on MPC Sample0.11.1 at88BPM with58% MIDI Swing.</p>
<video controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster={url('images/loop-club-scratch-0.11.1.webp')} aria-label="Loop Club Scratch Pocket: actual MPC Sample drum loop and fader scratch recording"><source src={p.scratchVideo} type="video/mp4"/>Download the Scratch Pocket performance below.</video>
<div class="manual-actions"><a href={p.scratchVideo}>Download Scratch Pocket</a><a href={url('mods/loop-club/manual/#turntable-scratch')}>Learn Turntable controls</a></div>
<p class="platform-note">Actual MPC Sample screen and USB audio, operated through remote controls. Original procedural drums and an original on-device synth recording; no commercial sample pack is used in this new demo.</p>
<h2>Earlier performances.</h2>
<h2>Hear it. Then play the effects.</h2>
<p>A short piece built on the MPC Sample, followed by live filter sweeps, repeat punches, reverse, drive/crush and tape-stop drops. This is actual device screen capture and USB output, triggered through remote controls. Song-building footage is from0.9.0; the updated FX section shows0.9.3 with direct parameter controls below the pads.</p>
<h3 id="full-performance">Full performance · 2:12</h3>
<p>Watch the complete session here: building the drum, bass, chord and melody loops, then performing with the effects. Live FX begins at 1:26.</p>
<video controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster={url('images/loop-club-performance-0.9.3.webp')} aria-label="Loop Club full MPC Sample song-building and live FX performance"><source src={p.fullVideo} type="video/mp4"/>Your browser can download the full performance below.</video>
<div class="manual-actions"><a href={p.fullVideo}>Download full performance (2:12)</a><a href={p.performanceVideo}>Watch or download FX only (46 seconds)</a></div>
<p class="platform-note">The demo uses the owner’s optional Cosmic Vintage drum bank. The download includes original procedural drums only; that commercial bank and its source samples are not distributed.</p>
<h2>New in 0.13.0.</h2>
<p>Tap PAD1 to toggle Turntable Grab. Hold PAD2 to cut only the scratch source, leaving the drum loop and mix level untouched. Input-cadence smoothing and zero-speed braking reduce abrupt stops and pitch fluctuations. The fader still moves the platter; K3 remains the track level.</p>
<p>TAP TEMPO sets the BPM; SHIFT+TAP toggles the monitor metronome. SETUP provides independent metronome and preroll switches, with four complete clicks for a one-bar count-in. ERASE/COPY also edits recorded Drum/CHOP notes while preserving their samples. Browser controls and all-page input ownership have been audited.</p>
<p>New projects use format12 and read formats1–11. Existing saved scratch trajectories retain their original curves. Keep a backup before saving: older versions cannot read format12.</p>
<h2>What this preview verifies.</h2>
<p>405 Debug tests, 31 focused optimized realtime/motion tests, strict Clippy, ARM64 builds and eight launcher checks pass. Actual MPC Sample screen and stereo USB checks cover Grab/Cut, navigation release, recording, recall and source preservation. Runtime and SD library hashes match the public ZIP.</p>
<p>Native replay of the preceding demonstration’s estimated input timings reduced near-stationary open-gate samples from12.68% to1.84%. That is a model comparison, not a physical-hand measurement. Smoothing adds following lag: the braking horizon is about40ms with50Hz input. Programmed sample-clock demonstrations separate engine behavior from network jitter; they do not certify turntable feel.</p>
<p>Physical controls, calibrated analog latency, power-cycle recovery and worst-case long-session load remain separate. The earlier detailed audit observed a scheduling-inclusive deadline crossing; this update does not establish unlimited CPU headroom.32shared synth/drum voices and16sampler voices remain shared limits.</p>
<h2>Know the boundaries.</h2>
<ul><li>USB currently exposes one stereo pair. MAIN / USB / MAIN+USB destinations do not provide individual drum USB stems.</li><li>USB-input recording, chromatic/chop MIDI capture and bounded Warp are included. XPM native inserts/envelopes/Warp and bank MIDI pattern import are not reproduced. GRID displays the first 64 events.</li><li>The download contains no commercial samples, personal expansions, firmware or QA management agent.</li><li>Source and SDK licenses are MIT. Follow the <a href={url('mods/loop-club/manual/')}>installation and recovery instructions</a> before changing your SD boot.</li></ul>
</article>
</Base>
